<article class="env-lemma" id="08BW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08BW">Lemma <span data-tag="08BW">20.33.3</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. Let $X = U \cup V$ be the union of two open subspaces of $X$. For objects $E$, $F$ of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ we have a Mayer-Vietoris sequence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ &  \ldots \ar[r] &  \mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^{-1}(E_{U \cap V}, F_{U \cap V}) \ar[lld] \\  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (E, F) \ar[r] &  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (E_ U, F_ U) \oplus \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (E_ V, F_ V) \ar[r] &  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits (E_{U \cap V}, F_{U \cap V}) }  \]
</div>
  <p> where the subscripts denote restrictions to the relevant opens and the $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits $'s and $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits $'s are taken in the relevant derived categories. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Use the distinguished triangle of Lemma <a href="/tag/08BU" data-tag="08BU">20.33.1</a> to obtain a long exact sequence of $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits $'s (from Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/0149" data-tag="0149">13.4.2</a>) and use that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{D(\mathcal{O}_ X)}(j_{U!}E|_ U, F) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{D(\mathcal{O}_ U)}(E|_ U, F|_ U)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Lemma <a href="/tag/08BT" data-tag="08BT">20.32.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>